1. e4 e5 2. d4 exd4 3. c3 dxc3 4. Bc4 cxb2 5. Bxb2 Qe7?! { Blocks the bishop's best square and walks into a quick lead for White, who is no longer worse. } 6. Nc3 { Develops and defends e4, so the black queen cannot take that pawn. The queen on e7 has blocked the bishop's best square. }
6... Nf6 7. Nge2 { Develops another piece and prepares to castle. White is now ahead in development with the pawn on e4 safe. }
7... d5 8. Nxd5 { Takes the pawn with the knight, since the bishop on c4 is not attacked. } 8... Nxd5 9. Bxd5 c6 10. Bb3 { Keeps the bishop on the diagonal and out of reach of ...c6. Plan: castle and bring the rooks to the centre. } 10... Be6?! 11. O-O { Puts the king safe and brings the rook to the open centre. } *
